#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; is a vocabulary application. It helps you to memorize your "
"vocabulary, for example when you are trying to learn a foreign language. You "
"can create your own files with the words you need or select from a great "
"range of files from the <ulink url=\"http://edu.kde.org/parley\">homepage</"
"ulink>. There you can find files containing language vocabulary and also "
"anatomy, music, geography, chemistry or exam preparation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; is very flexible and uses the flash card learning approach. It "
"automatically keeps track of your progress and lets you sort your vocabulary "
"as you wish. Unlike with real flash cards you can use different learning "
"methods with &parley;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You probably remember flashcards from school. The card would contain the "
"original expression on the front side of the card and the translation on the "
"back. Then you look at the cards one after another. If you knew the "
"translation, you could put it away. If you failed, you put it back to try "
"again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; is not intended to teach you grammar or other sophisticated things. "
"This is, and probably will stay, beyond the scope of this application."
msgstr ""

