#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you can see below, the entries of the vocabulary are arranged similar to "
"a spreadsheet. On the left are the lessons containing the vocabulary. "
"<screenshot> <mediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"parley-main-"
"water.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> <textobject><phrase>Screenshot</"
"phrase></textobject> </mediaobject> </screenshot> In the picture above, you "
"can see the main window of parley. It contains two important areas: The "
"lesson list on the left and the actual vocabulary on the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "The lesson list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The lesson list is on the left and shows you which lessons you document "
"contains."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One lesson is the current one, it is indicated by the colored bar over it. "
"In this case it is survival training."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A checkmark next to a lesson indicates that it is to be included in the "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Above the list you find a combo box which lets you select which vocabulary "
"you want displayed on the right:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current lesson only (survival training in this case)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lessons in the test (the ones with a checkmark)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "All lessons (everything in the document)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "The vocabulary list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The vocabulary list is on the right. Depending on your selection which "
"lesson to edit the entries of one or more lessons are displayed here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A green check mark in the second columns means that this line is active. A "
"red cross indicates a deactivated entry that will never be practiced. See "
"Editing Entries for more information on active entries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you mark a range of entries to work with, they appear with a different "
"background. Many editing functions work for multiple entries at the same "
"time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The color in the column with the original will vary if you have two or more "
"columns with translations. If the cursor is in one of the translations the "
"color represents its grade <quote>to the original</quote>. See section <link "
"linkend=\"entry6-dlg\">entry dialog</link> for more on this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course it is also possible to use it as an ordinary dictionary and <link "
"linkend=\"smart-search\">lookup manually</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "The search bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "The search bar is located above the vocabulary table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the search bar to filter you vocabulary. Type in a word and see "
"how only entries containing the word are shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr "Ecran"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "The status bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the bottom of the main window you also see the status line. It usually "
"contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "The word type (for example: noun/verb/adjective)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How to pronounce this expression. You can use <acronym>IPA</acronym> "
"characters from the phonetic alphabet. See more about this in the according "
"<link linkend=\"opt-dlg-ipa\">options dialog page</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "A comment that can be added to an entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the keyboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I tried to optimize the work flow for the use with the keyboard. So all of "
"the important functions are reachable this way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Tab</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor is moved to the smart search input field. If you start typing an "
"expression in this field, &parley; will search the next best match after "
"each key. The cursor in the vocabulary is then moved to this location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you press <keycap>Return</keycap> it will move to the next match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you only want entries that match from the <emphasis>beginning</emphasis> "
"of the expression you must press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; "
"<keycap>Return</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift; <keycap>Tab</keycap></keycombo> "
"or <keycap>Tab</keycap> will move back to the vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved one column to the left. If it has "
"reached the leftmost column, nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved one column to the right. If it has "
"reached the rightmost column, nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid "Up Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved one row upwards. If it has reached the "
"topmost row, nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Down Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved one row downwards. If it has reached "
"the bottommost row, nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page Up"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved one page (the amount of visible lines -"
"1) upwards. If the cursor would exceed the first possible row, nothing "
"happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page Down"
msgstr "Pagina d'aval"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cursor in the vocabulary is moved one page downwards. If the cursor "
"would exceed the last possible row, nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycombo
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Ctrl;<keycap>Return</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Invoke the <guilabel>Edit Properties</guilabel> dialog for modification of "
"this entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Ins</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Appends a new row at the end of the vocabulary. The cursor is moved to the "
"entry in the <guilabel>Original</guilabel> row. Edit the items in place or "
"invoke the <guilabel>Edit Properties</guilabel> dialog for modification of "
"this entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have selected smart appending you are prompted to enter originals and "
"their translations until you stop by pressing the ESC key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Del</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After confirmation of a safety dialog, the currently selected row or "
"selection is removed from the vocabulary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> or <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By pressing &Ctrl; and one of the two number pad keys, <keycap>+</keycap> or "
"<keycap>-</keycap>, you can choose the previous or next item in the combo "
"box determining the current lesson. If you do not have a number pad you may "
"also use the normal <keycap>+</keycap> or <keycap>-</keycap> keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double clicking an expression in the table lets you edit this items in place."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<mousebutton>Left</mousebutton> mouse click in of the header buttons will "
"sort this column in ascending order. The next click will sort in descending "
"order. When the column is sorted you can see a triangle in the button that "
"shows the direction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keeping pressed the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse button for about 1 "
"second in on of the table header buttons will pop up its <link linkend="
"\"header-menu\">header menu</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working on selections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is possible to mark a range of expressions. You can then modify one or "
"more properties from the selection or save them as a new file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on an entry, the whole row is marked for further processing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you keep the &Ctrl; key pressed while clicking on an entry, the whole row "
"is added to yoor selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you additionally press a &Shift; key when clicking on an entry, the "
"selection will be extended from the current entry to the previously selected "
"entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You invoke the edit dialog to modify the selection by pressing <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Return</keycap></keycombo>. In this case the "
"dialog appears differently. Some properties are disabled. For example it "
"does not make sense to edit the expression itself or the remark of a whole "
"range."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All selectable fields are empty at the beginning to represent the unmodified "
"state. Once you have modified a property there will be contents in its field "
"and only those properties are altered in your selection when you confirm the "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available file formats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid "&parley; can read and write the following file formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Its native xml-style document type with the extension <literal role="
"\"extension\">.kvtml</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to share documents with others use this one as it is the only "
"file format that is capable of containing <emphasis>all</emphasis> the "
"properties in &parley;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simple text files with special delimiters between the entries which are also "
"used by simple database programs. The extension is <literal role=\"extension"
"\">csv</literal> in this case."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a lot of files on the Internet which use the tabular character or "
"one or two colons to separate the different languages. To select this "
"separator use the tab for setting the <link linkend=\"options4-dlg"
"\"><guilabel> Copy &amp; Paste</guilabel> options</link> in the "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &parley;...</guimenuitem> "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; reads the first few bytes from a file and makes a guess about the "
"file format. When none of the special types like <literal role=\"extension"
"\">kvtml</literal> or <literal role=\"extension\">lex</literal> are "
"recognized, it uses the <literal role=\"extension\">csv</literal> format."
msgstr ""

