#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "And how should I learn?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The usual way to learn with &parley; is to use one of its random query "
"functions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It keeps track of your knowledge of the expressions by assigning them one of "
"seven grades ranging from <quote>Level 1</quote> to <quote>Level 7</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Several possibilities are implemented which can be configured in the dialog "
"for the query options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To keep the amount of expressions reasonable, restrict the query to a lesson "
"and/or a word type. I personally prefer about 50 words per cycle and "
"subdivide the lessons accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore, the range for the query can depend on the current grade, the "
"number of queries and the last query date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Learning is efficient, if you do not repeat the words for a certain length "
"of time, depending on the current grade."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a blocking and expiring mechanism for that case, so you are not "
"obliged to modify the settings after each cycle. The known expression is "
"blocked at least for the given time and will be shown after the expiration "
"time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:670
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The direction of the learning can be changed randomly to avoid one way "
"learning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:673
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For your personal taste or just for becoming acquainted with a new word, you "
"can choose a query that shows the solution together with several other "
"randomly chosen words (called multiple choice)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:678
#, no-c-format
msgid "Special word types need special queries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:679
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For this reason there are queries for the conjugation of verbs, comparison "
"form of adjectives and the articles of nouns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All these settings can be summarized into <link linkend=\"profiles"
"\">profiles</link> and retained under an arbitrarily name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When querying &parley; shows the expressions in random order until you "
"confirm all as <quote>known</quote>. If you did not select a special lesson, "
"all lessons are queried one after the other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remaining expressions of a currently running query are accordingly stored "
"when you leave &parley;. After a later restart you can resume the query "
"(currently this does not apply to special queries with verbs, articles and "
"comparisons). Those expressions are marked with a green check mark in the "
"<link linkend=\"overview\">main view</link>."
msgstr ""

