#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open this dialog with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure &parley;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. The settings "
"in this dialog are global and affect all vocabularies equally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:889 index.docbook:1911
#, no-c-format
msgid "General"
msgstr "General"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:892
#, no-c-format
msgid "General settings dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:895
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Settings Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:901
#, no-c-format
msgid "Save vocabularies automatically on close and quit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you check this option, &parley; will automatically save the document if "
"it was modified when you use the close button or when you quit &parley;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:904 index.docbook:915
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As a side effect it also does not ask for confirmation to save when quitting "
"with modified data but saves the vocabulary without asking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:911
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a backup every 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:912
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; will automatically save the document if it was modified after the "
"period you enter here when the option is checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:918
#, no-c-format
msgid "An interval of 0 also stops this behavior."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid "Smart appending"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this feature is activated, you will repeatedly be prompted with the entry "
"dialog. After entering the first original you have to enter the "
"corresponding translations. Afterwards you proceed with the next original "
"and its translations until you stop by pressing the &Esc; key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are in this mode and modify the lesson in the dialog it has the "
"same meaning as selecting the lesson in the toolbar. This way it is "
"preselected when the next entry dialog appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The required lessons will have to be created in advance in the document "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid "Apply changes without asking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:937
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, all options are save upon termination of &parley;. Otherwise "
"you have to select the appropriate menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid "Column Resizing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:945
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you resize your main window it is convenient, if the columns resize "
"automatically, too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:947
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is possible in two manners:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:950
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "Automatic"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:951
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&parley; makes each columns the same width except the leftmost with the "
"lesson names which has half the size of the others. The second column which "
"contains the picture that describes the state of the row has a fixed width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:958
#, no-c-format
msgid "Percentage"
msgstr "Percentatge"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:959
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The widths of the columns are altered with the same factor the main window "
"grew or shrunk."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:966
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the last button labeled <guilabel>Fixed</guilabel> is set, no resizing of "
"the columns is done."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:974
#, no-c-format
msgid "Languages"
msgstr "Lengas"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:977
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Language Settings</guilabel> dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Language Settings</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:986
#, no-c-format
msgid "Language code"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:987
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each column can be assigned a language. This is internally done with the "
"usual <ulink url=\"http://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/englangn.html"
"\">international language codes</ulink> &eg; <literal>en</literal>, "
"<literal>de</literal>, <literal>it</literal>. These codes are also stored "
"with the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:992
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should always use the correct codes to be able to share vocabularies "
"with others. Merging vocabularies also relies on the correct language codes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:998
#, no-c-format
msgid "Alternative code"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:999
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes it may be useful to have a second language code because some "
"languages have the usual short code and one or two longer codes. For German "
"for example it is common to use <literal>de</literal> but either "
"<literal>deu</literal> or <literal>ger</literal> is also possible according "
"to ISO639-2."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid "Language name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can give the language code a descriptive name in your own language "
"which is shown in the header buttons in the <link linkend=\"overview\">main "
"view</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1015
#, no-c-format
msgid "Picture"
msgstr "Imatge"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1016
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally you can add a nice icon to your language which is shown in the "
"table header button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1018
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; 2 stores those pixmaps under <filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/"
"locale/l10n/<replaceable>language -code</replaceable></filename>."
msgstr ""

