msgid ""
"Lets you choose a font to display the characters from the international "
"phonetic alphabet. This is used to show the pronunciation of the expression "
"on the bottom in the statusbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1098
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Probably you do not have an IPA enabled font since those characters are "
"seldom used. You may download a free font from <ulink url=\"http://"
"bibliofile.mc.duke.edu/gww/fonts/Unicode.html\">http://bibliofile.mc.duke."
"edu/gww/fonts/Unicode.html </ulink> or <ulink url=\"http://www.hclrss.demon."
"co.uk/unicode/fonts.html\">http://www.hclrss.demon.co.uk/unicode/fonts.html "
"</ulink>. Install these fonts for example with kfontinst."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have <application>StarOffice</application> installed you probably "
"have the font <quote>Lucida Sans Unicode</quote> which also contains most of "
"the needed characters (but be sure to select the font which ends with "
"<quote>Unicode</quote>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I also found a <ulink url=\"http://esl.about.com/library/weekly/aa040998.htm"
"\"> Reference and Introduction to Phonetic Symbols</ulink> that explains a "
"bit about the background. There is also <ulink url=\"http://www2.arts.gla.ac."
"uk/IPA/ipa.html\"> The International Phonetic Association</ulink> where you "
"can find even more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Grade Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every grade can be assigned an individual color. For example I prefer green "
"for best grade and red for worst."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want any colors but just black on white, uncheck the "
"<guilabel>Use Colors</guilabel> check box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy &amp; Paste"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:1135
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Copy &amp; Paste Settings</guilabel> dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:1138
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Copy &amp; Paste Settings</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Separator"
msgstr "Separador"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a sequence of one ore more characters which divide the parts of an "
"expression when transferring data from or to an other application over the "
"clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most common item is <keycap>TAB</keycap> which uses the tabulator "
"character. Another possibility is to use the semicolon, if you want to "
"export data to a database file in <literal role=\"extension\">CSV</literal> "
"format.This character is also used to read such files correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Order"
msgstr "Òrdre"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When pasting via the clipboard &parley; does not know which languages the "
"different fields belong to and just would insert them from left to right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To facilitate correct behavior, if you arranged your vocabulary in an other "
"way, you can determine your desired order with this area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The buttons right to the list box move the current language up or down. "
"<guibutton>Skip</guibutton> will insert a hole which means that the later "
"calculated field from the clipboard is skipped."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use current document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, the items in the clipboard are assumed to be in the same "
"language order as the current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Query"
msgstr "Consulta"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:1178
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Query Settings</guilabel> dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:1181
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Query Settings</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Time Per Query"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can influence the behavior of &parley; when you do not know the "
"answer in time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may set a time limit &parley; grants you to remember the correct answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally you can tell &parley; what to do when this limit is reached. "
"Besides of waiting unlimited time you may select to be shown the solution or "
"to continue immediately with the next question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore you can activate a little progress bar to show the remaining "
"time for the current answer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you exceed the time limit several times in series in continuous mode "
"&parley; will assume that there is currently no person in front of the "
"screen and stop the query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Swap direction randomly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually a query is only in one direction, depending on the column you used "
"to start the query. With this check box you can determine, that the "
"directions are altered randomly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1214
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use alternative learning method"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The normal learning style is to learn a single lesson at a time, and when "
"you answer correctly the first time it is removed from the current learning "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The alternative method was developed by Sebastian Leitner in his book \"So "
"lernt man lernen, Angewandte Lernpsychologie - ein Weg zum Erfolg"
"\" (Freiburg: Heider, 1972) (English: Learn how to learn, applied learning "
"psychology - A way to success)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The idea of Leitner's method is to try learn those questions you have a hard "
"time to learn, and do not bother you with those that you do know. This is "
"accomplished by requiring you to answer correctly to each question four "
"times in a row."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In real life it works by creating four rows of cards. Each row, above the "
"bottom one, can only hold a certain number of cards. The top row can hold "
"seven cards, the others can hold two cards. (In the original game, the "
"bottom row can only hold three card, thus limiting the number of cards in "
"the game to 20. This \"limitation\" is not present in &parley;.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the bottom row are the questions that have yet to be asked and the "
"questions that have previously been answered incorrectly. When a question is "
"answered correctly, it is removed from the row it was in and moved to the "
"back of row above. If answered incorrectly, the card is moved to the back of "
"the bottom row. If the row a card is placed in exceed the maximum number of "
"cards for that row, the next question is taken from the front of that row, "
"else the question is taken from the front of the bottom row. A card is "
"removed from the game when it would otherwise be moved to the fifth row, "
"&ie; it has been answering correctly while located in the top row."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Thresholds"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:1257
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Thresholds Settings</guilabel> dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:1260
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Thresholds Settings</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog you determine which entries are included in the next "
"selection for random query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have activated the blocking mechanism on the next dialog page, the "
"thresholds from <guilabel>Grade</guilabel>, <guilabel>Query count</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>Bad count</guilabel> and <guilabel>Last query</"
"guilabel> are disabled and not taken into account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1278 index.docbook:1434
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lesson"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Designate which lessons to include or leave out. An arbitrary number of "
"lessons can be selected for the calculation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For convenience there are two additional buttons to selected all entries or "
"none."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Starting with version 0.7.0 this part is stored with the document instead of "
"storing globally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Word type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1289
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the word type. &parley; does not pay any attention to subtypes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1294 index.docbook:1638
#, no-c-format
msgid "Grade"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1295
#, no-c-format
msgid "The same for the grade."
msgstr ""

