#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1413
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you enter a new expression into a table cell or modify existing entries "
"and their properties. This dialog is accessed when a cell is chosen and you "
"select <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Edit Selected Area..."
"</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menu or the <guibutton>Edit "
"Expression...</guibutton> button in the <guilabel>Random Query</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:1420
#, no-c-format
msgid "Entry dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:1423
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Entry dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expression"
msgstr "Expression"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1430
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contains your words."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1435
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects the desired lesson."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button on the right also invokes the <guilabel>Edit Lesson Names</"
"guilabel> dialog where you can edit lessons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1441
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pronunciation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1442
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this field you can describe how the word is pronounced."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is possible either by using simple ascii characters and maybe an fancy "
"and very personal phonetic description or better by using the international "
"phonetic alphabet. The button on the right invokes a <link linkend=\"pron-"
"window\">dialog</link> where you can select all the characters that belong "
"to this alphabet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type"
msgstr "Tipe"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Lets you choose one of the predefined types for your expression. If you "
"change the type for an entry, all the other entries in that row will be "
"assigned the new type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1459
#, no-c-format
msgid "See the table for all <link linkend=\"types\">available types</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1464
#, no-c-format
msgid "Subtype"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some types also include subtypes. If there is no subtype available this "
"field is disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1467
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every entry in a row can have a different subtype. This is useful for nouns "
"as the gender of a noun may be different in different languages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button to the right of this field invokes the <guilabel>Edit User "
"Defined Types</guilabel> dialog so you can edit the <guilabel>Type "
"Descriptions</guilabel> immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1475
#, no-c-format
msgid "Usage Labels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1476
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One or more usage labels can be selected to describe the usual usage of the "
"expression, &eg; medicine or chemistry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1478
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button on the right invokes the the <guilabel>Edit User-Defined Usage "
"Labels</guilabel> dialog to enter a new usage label."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1484
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting from the international phonetic alphabet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have an IPA-enabled font installed your dialog should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:1490
#, no-c-format
msgid "IPA dialog screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:1493
#, no-c-format
